    {
      "ts": "2026-02-15T10:38:39.300-08:00",
      "player": "DSV3 Libby",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "Interesting. I can target my opponent's Stormchaser's Talent, my own Stormchaser's Talent, or my Duelists. Let me think about this strategically:\n\
\n\
1. I could bounce my opponent's Stormchaser's Talent to disrupt their plan\n\
2. I could bounce my own Duelist to draw a card (since I control it) and potentially replay it next turn\n\
3. I could bounce my own Stormchaser's Talent to reset it or draw a card\n\
\n\
Since I control any permanent I target, I'll draw a card. Let me check the rules for Stormchaser's Talent again. It's a Class enchantment - if I bounce my own, I'll lose the level 1 ability and have to start over, but I'll draw a card. If I bounce a Duelist, I'll draw a card and can replay it next turn.\n\
\n\
