  "annotations": [
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "The player has 2 untapped lands and several castable spells but chose to do nothing. Gran-Gran costs {U} and could be cast, providing a body on board and its looting ability when tapped. Artist's Talent costs {1}{R} and could also be cast to enable card filtering. Boomerang Basics could bounce the opponent's Otter token. Firebending Lesson could kill the opponent's 1/1 Otter token. Passing the turn with 2 mana available and multiple playable options wastes tempo in an early game where board development matters. At minimum, Gran-Gran should have been cast as a 1/2 body that generates card selection and enables future cost reduction with Lessons in graveyard.",
      "action_taken": "Passed the turn without casting any spells, leaving 2 mana unused.",
      "better_line": "Cast Gran-Gran for {U}, developing the board with a creature that has relevant abilities (looting when tapped, cost reduction with Lessons in graveyard). Could also consider Artist's Talent for {1}{R} to enable card filtering, or Firebending Lesson to remove opponent's Otter token.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 22,
      "player": "Sonnet Stoic",
      "decision_index": 15,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Playing Riverpyre Verge now means Spirebluff Canal will likely be the 4th land played (entering tapped), losing tempo on a critical turn. Spirebluff Canal enters untapped only with 2 or fewer other lands, so it should be played earlier.",
      "action_taken": "Played Riverpyre Verge as 2nd land",
      "better_line": "Play Spirebluff Canal as the 2nd land (enters untapped), preserving Island and Riverpyre Verge for later turns when Spirebluff would enter tapped",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 25,
      "player": "DSV3 Libby",
      "decision_index": 18,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Duelist of the Mind has flying and vigilance, meaning it can attack for 1 damage through the air with zero downside (stays untapped to block). The opponent has no flyers to block it. This is free damage left on the table.",
      "action_taken": "Attacked with only the Otter Token, leaving Duelist of the Mind back despite having vigilance.",
      "better_line": "Attack with both Otter Token and Duelist of the Mind. Duelist has flying (can't be blocked by opponent's Otter) and vigilance (no downside to attacking).",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 29,
      "player": "DSV3 Libby",
      "decision_index": 21,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Casting Duelist of the Mind in the precombat main phase is suboptimal. The existing Duelist of the Mind on the battlefield has power equal to cards drawn this turn, and casting spells/creatures before combat doesn't increase its power. More importantly, Frostcliff Siege (choosing Jeskai) would be a stronger play here - it provides card advantage whenever creatures deal combat damage. With a Duelist of the Mind already on board (flying, vigilance), casting Frostcliff Siege before combat would let the Duelist attack and draw a card immediately this turn. The second Duelist of the Mind entering as a 0/3 (having drawn 0 cards this turn) doesn't contribute to combat this turn. Additionally, casting the creature before combat when holding Boomerang Basics (a trick/noncreature spell) means missing the opportunity to sequence optimally - playing Frostcliff Siege would also trigger Artist's Talent-style synergies with the Stormchaser's Talent otter's prowess.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Duelist of the Mind (second copy) in precombat main phase",
      "better_line": "Cast Frostcliff Siege choosing Jeskai before combat, then attack with the existing Duelist of the Mind and Otter token to trigger the Jeskai draw ability. The second Duelist could be cast post-combat or on a later turn.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 38,
      "player": "DSV3 Libby",
      "decision_index": 27,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Discarded Quantum Riddler instead of Frostcliff Siege, despite reasoning that concluded Frostcliff Siege should be discarded. Quantum Riddler has Warp {1}{U} making it castable cheaply as a 2/2, but Frostcliff Siege (Jeskai mode) provides a consistent card draw engine that synergizes extremely well with two flying Duelist of the Mind on board - each combat damage trigger draws a card, which directly pumps Duelist power. However, the Riddler's Warp ability and late-game potential also have value, making this a close call.",
      "action_taken": "Discarded Quantum Riddler",
      "better_line": "Discard Frostcliff Siege or Boomerang Basics. Keeping Quantum Riddler for Warp {1}{U} as a cheap creature, while Frostcliff Siege competes with other 3-mana plays. Actually, keeping Frostcliff Siege for its synergy with Duelists is likely better.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 45,
      "player": "DSV3 Libby",
      "decision_index": 34,
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "With 3 mana available (UUG from Steam Vents + 2x Willowrush Verge), casting Stormchaser's Talent for U is fine value, but the sequencing and choice could be debated. The opponent has two Duelist of the Mind on board which are threatening. Boomerang Basics (U) could bounce one of the Duelists, which is a tempo play that also draws a card since it's the opponent's permanent being returned (no, it only draws if you controlled it). Gran-Gran (U) is a 1/2 that loots when tapped AND reduces noncreature spell costs with 3+ Lessons in graveyard - important synergy with the Lesson-heavy hand. However, casting Stormchaser's Talent to get a 1/1 prowess blocker is reasonable given the two Duelists threatening in the air. The main concern is whether Artist's Talent (1R) could have been cast - with UUG available, there's no R source unless Steam Vents taps for R. Steam Vents can tap for U or R, so the player could cast Artist's Talent (1R = using Steam Vents for R + Willowrush for U). Artist's Talent provides looting on noncreature spells which is strong with this hand full of noncreature spells. But Stormchaser's Talent gives a body to block the Duelists and leaves mana open for Firebending Lesson to kill a Duelist. Actually, casting Stormchaser's Talent for U leaves UG open - not enough for Firebending Lesson (R). So this sequencing doesn't enable holding up removal. The play is defensible but there were arguments for other lines.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Stormchaser's Talent to create a 1/1 Otter with prowess",
      "better_line": "Consider casting Gran-Gran (U) first as a blocker that also provides card filtering, or casting Artist's Talent (1R using Steam Vents for R) to set up the looting engine for future turns with a hand full of noncreature spells. Alternatively, holding up Steam Vents for R to cast Firebending Lesson on a Duelist of the Mind (which has 3 toughness, so only 2 damage wouldn't kill it) - though that doesn't work either. Stormchaser's Talent is a reasonable choice.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 52,
      "player": "Sonnet Stoic",
      "decision_index": 40,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Willowrush Verge has an unconditional '{T}: Add {U}' ability. The player incorrectly believed they only had G available, missing that they could cast either Boomerang Basics or Stormchaser's Talent. Bouncing an opponent's Duelist of the Mind with Boomerang Basics while the opponent is completely tapped out would have been a strong tempo play, removing a key threat.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without casting anything, believing only G mana was available.",
      "better_line": "Tap Willowrush Verge for U and cast Boomerang Basics targeting one of the opponent's Duelist of the Mind to remove a threat while opponent is tapped out, or cast Stormchaser's Talent for another Otter token.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 56,
      "player": "Sonnet Stoic",
      "decision_index": 42,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Passed without casting Frostcliff Siege before combat. Either Temur mode (giving the summoning-sick Duelist haste to attack, plus +1/+0 and trample to both Duelists) or Jeskai mode (drawing cards on combat damage) would have been significantly better cast precombat rather than held. Passing loses the benefit of the enchantment for this turn's combat.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without casting any spells in precombat main phase",
      "better_line": "Cast Frostcliff Siege choosing Temur to give both Duelists +1/+0, trample, and haste (enabling the summoning-sick one to attack), then attack with both",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 60,
      "player": "DSV3 Libby",
      "decision_index": 45,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Declined to cast Boomerang Basics with 2 untapped lands available. Bouncing opponent's Stormchaser's Talent (their key enchantment engine) would have been a strong tempo play, forcing them to spend mana replaying it. Alternatively, bouncing the Otter Token removes their only blocker for next turn's attacks.",
      "action_taken": "Passed without casting any spells in postcombat main",
      "better_line": "Cast Boomerang Basics targeting opponent's Stormchaser's Talent to remove their enchantment engine and gain tempo advantage, or target the Otter Token to remove their only blocker",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 71,
      "player": "DSV3 Libby",
      "decision_index": 58,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Casting a second Stormchaser's Talent when already having one on the battlefield is low value - the legendary rule doesn't apply to Classes, but the first level ability just creates another 1/1 Otter. Meanwhile, Sonnet Stoic is at 11 life facing two Duelist of the Mind (which can be very large with card draw), and has Boomerang Basics available to bounce one of those Duelists. Additionally, Artist's Talent at 1R would provide a much stronger value engine (loot on noncreature spells, and can level up for cost reduction). The sequencing is also questionable - they should consider bouncing a Duelist first to stabilize, or casting Artist's Talent for ongoing value rather than getting a second 1/1 token that won't meaningfully help against the opponent's flyers.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Stormchaser's Talent to create a second 1/1 Otter token",
      "better_line": "Cast Boomerang Basics targeting one of the opponent's Duelist of the Mind to remove a key threat, or cast Artist's Talent (1R) for a stronger ongoing value engine. Bouncing a Duelist is especially important since they have flying and vigilance, making them difficult to race.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 76,
      "player": "Sonnet Stoic",
      "decision_index": 61,
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "At 11 life facing two Duelist of the Mind with flying, bouncing the opponent's Stormchaser's Talent instead of a Duelist removes a value engine but doesn't address the immediate flying damage clock. Stormchaser's Talent only costs U to replay, while bouncing a Duelist (costs 1U to replay) would directly reduce incoming damage and buy more time.",
      "action_taken": "Bounced opponent's Stormchaser's Talent",
      "better_line": "Bounce one of the two Duelist of the Mind to reduce the flying damage clock while at 11 life. The Duelist is the immediate threat and costs more to replay.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 79,
      "player": "Sonnet Stoic",
      "decision_index": 63,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "DSV3 Libby passed their precombat main with 4 untapped lands and strong plays available. Fear of Missing Out (1R) would ETB loot (increasing Duelist of the Mind's power via the draw), create a 2/3 attacker, and with delirium active (5+ card types in graveyard), grant extra combat phases. Stormchaser's Talent could also create another token. The opponent is at 11 life with all lands tapped and only two small Otter tokens as defense.",
      "action_taken": "Passed precombat main without casting any spells",
      "better_line": "Cast Fear of Missing Out (1R) precombat to get the loot trigger (boosting Duelist's power), add a 2/3 body, and leverage delirium for extra combat phases. Could also consider casting Stormchaser's Talent for another token or Boomerang Basics to clear a blocker.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 84,
      "player": "DSV3 Libby",
      "decision_index": 66,
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Combustion Technique would deal 4 damage (2 base + 2 Lessons in graveyard: Boomerang Basics x2) to Duelist of the Mind (0-power/3 toughness with flying and vigilance), cleanly killing and exiling it. Removing this flying vigilance threat would free up the Otters to attack more effectively and prevent future Duelist value. Artist's Talent builds long-term value but doesn't address the board threat.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Artist's Talent to build enchantment value engine",
      "better_line": "Cast Combustion Technique targeting Duelist of the Mind to remove the flying vigilance threat (4 damage vs 3 toughness), still triggering prowess on both Otters, then cast Artist's Talent on a future turn",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 87,
      "player": "Sonnet Stoic",
      "decision_index": 68,
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Attacking both 1/1 Otter tokens into a Duelist of the Mind (1/3 with vigilance) means one Otter will trade for just 1 point of chip damage getting through. At 11 life vs opponent's 20 life, trading a prowess creature for 1 damage is a poor rate. The Otters have prowess and could become meaningful threats when casting spells later.",
      "action_taken": "Attacked with both Otter Tokens into a Duelist of the Mind with vigilance, losing one Otter for 1 damage.",
      "better_line": "Attack with just one Otter (or neither) to preserve the prowess tokens for a turn where you can cast spells pre-combat to pump them, or hold them back as blockers given the life deficit.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 89,
      "player": "Sonnet Stoic",
      "decision_index": 68,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "DSV3 Libby passed priority precombat with Duelist of the Mind on board (currently 0/3 power). Casting spells that draw cards precombat would pump Duelist's power for the attack. Fear of Missing Out (1R) would trigger a draw, and with 5 card types in graveyard enabling delirium, would grant an extra combat phase with untap. Boomerang Basics targeting an opponent's permanent would trigger Duelist's crime ability for another draw. Combined, Duelist could attack as a 2/3 or 3/3 across multiple combats against a tapped-out opponent at 11 life.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without casting any spells precombat, leaving Duelist of the Mind at 0 power for combat.",
      "better_line": "Cast Fear of Missing Out precombat (triggers draw via ETB, enabling delirium extra combat), then cast Boomerang Basics targeting an opponent's permanent (triggering Duelist's crime ability for another draw). Attack with pumped Duelist across multiple combat phases.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 93,
      "player": "DSV3 Libby",
      "decision_index": 74,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Casting Duelist of the Mind (a creature) before combat instead of casting noncreature spells first to pump the existing Duelist of the Mind's power. Boomerang Basics targeting an opponent's Stormchaser's Talent or Otter Token would trigger the crime ability on the existing Duelist (draw + discard), increasing its power for combat. With opponent completely tapped out, there's no reason to hold back.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Duelist of the Mind (creature) as first spell in precombat main phase",
      "better_line": "Cast Boomerang Basics targeting opponent's Stormchaser's Talent first (crime triggers Duelist draw, pumping its power), then potentially cast second Boomerang Basics on another target, then attack with a powered-up Duelist, then cast Duelist of the Mind post-combat",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 105,
      "player": "DSV3 Libby",
      "decision_index": 85,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Only attacked with one Duelist of the Mind when both Duelists have flying and vigilance. Both could attack for free since vigilance means they stay untapped for blocking, and flying means the opponent's tapped Otter Tokens couldn't block anyway. This wastes damage against an opponent at 11 life.",
      "action_taken": "Attacked with only one Duelist of the Mind",
      "better_line": "Attack with both Duelists of the Mind ('All attack') since both have flying and vigilance, making the attack completely free with no defensive downside",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 107,
      "player": "DSV3 Libby",
      "decision_index": 85,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Bounced Gran-Gran (a cheap 1-mana creature that can easily be replayed) instead of Artist's Talent, which is a much higher-value enchantment that likely has level-up investment. Artist's Talent at higher levels provides cost reduction and +2 noncombat damage, making it the most impactful permanent to bounce for tempo. Alternatively, a leveled-up Stormchaser's Talent would also be a better target.",
      "action_taken": "Targeted Gran-Gran with Boomerang Basics",
      "better_line": "Target Artist's Talent with Boomerang Basics to reset its level progress and remove the most impactful permanent from the board",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 113,
      "player": "DSV3 Libby",
      "decision_index": 94,
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "With delirium already active (creature, land, sorcery, enchantment, instant in graveyard), Fear of Missing Out would enable extra combat phases on future turns alongside two Duelists of the Mind, which could be devastating. The 2/3 body is also more impactful than a 1/1 Otter token.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Stormchaser's Talent for U, creating a 1/1 Otter with prowess",
      "better_line": "Cast Fear of Missing Out for 1R to get a 2/3 body with loot ETB and enable extra combat phases with active delirium, maximizing the two Duelists of the Mind on board",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 115,
      "player": "DSV3 Libby",
      "decision_index": 95,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "With Sonnet Stoic at 8 life and two Duelist of the Mind ready to attack, bouncing Toph (a 3/4 blocker that costs 4 mana to replay) would have been more impactful than bouncing Artist's Talent (a value enchantment). Removing the biggest blocker enables more combat damage to push toward lethal, and the tempo loss of replaying a 4-mana creature is much larger than replaying a 2-mana enchantment.",
      "action_taken": "Bounced Artist's Talent, removing a value engine but leaving Toph as a 3/4 blocker.",
      "better_line": "Bounce Toph, Hardheaded Teacher to remove the largest blocker and maximize combat damage with the opponent at 8 life.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 127,
      "player": "DSV3 Libby",
      "decision_index": 111,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Toph (3/4) was held back from attacking despite being unable to block the opponent's primary threats (two Duelist of the Mind with flying). Toph attacking would either deal 3 damage or force a favorable trade with a 0/3 Duelist. Keeping Toph back provides no defensive value against flying creatures.",
      "action_taken": "Attacked with only the two Otter Tokens, keeping Toph back on defense.",
      "better_line": "Attack with all three creatures (both Otter Tokens and Toph). Toph can't block flyers anyway, so there's no defensive reason to hold it back, and it represents 3 additional damage or forces a favorable block.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 136,
      "player": "Sonnet Stoic",
      "decision_index": 114,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "At 8 life facing two flying Duelist of the Mind with vigilance, the priority should be removing a Duelist rather than deploying a 1/2 ground creature. Combustion Technique would deal 4 damage (2 base + 2 Lessons in graveyard) to kill a Duelist, significantly reducing the flying clock. Gran-Gran doesn't block flyers and doesn't address the immediate survival concern.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Gran-Gran, a 1/2 ground creature that doesn't interact with the opponent's flying threats.",
      "better_line": "Cast Combustion Technique targeting one of the Duelist of the Mind to remove a flying threat. If mana permits, also cast Gran-Gran afterward.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 140,
      "player": "Sonnet Stoic",
      "decision_index": 118,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "At 8 life facing two flying Duelist of the Mind with vigilance, Sonnet Stoic chose to cast Artist's Talent for long-term value instead of using Combustion Technique to kill one of the Duelists. Combustion Technique would deal 4 damage (2 base + 2 Lessons in graveyard), enough to kill a 3-toughness Duelist. With flying threats putting significant pressure at low life, removing a threat is much more important than building incremental value.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Artist's Talent for long-term value enchantment",
      "better_line": "Cast Combustion Technique targeting one of the Duelist of the Mind to remove a flying threat while at 8 life",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 142,
      "player": "Sonnet Stoic",
      "decision_index": 120,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Duelist of the Mind has vigilance, so it doesn't tap when attacking and is already untapped. Targeting it with Fear of Missing Out's untap trigger accomplishes nothing. Fear of Missing Out itself is tapped from attacking and could be untapped to attack again in the additional combat phase for 2 extra damage against an opponent at 8 life.",
      "action_taken": "Targeted Duelist of the Mind with the untap trigger, which was already untapped due to vigilance.",
      "better_line": "Target Fear of Missing Out to untap it, allowing it to attack again in the additional combat phase for 2 extra damage.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 150,
      "player": "DSV3 Libby",
      "decision_index": 128,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Gran-Gran is a valuable creature (card filtering + potential cost reduction with Lessons), and the earthbent Willowrush Verge would return to the battlefield tapped when it dies due to earthbend's ability. Blocking with Willowrush Verge instead of Gran-Gran would save the same amount of life while preserving the more valuable permanent.",
      "action_taken": "Planned to block a Duelist with Gran-Gran (losing Gran-Gran) and block another attacker with Toph.",
      "better_line": "Block one attacker with Toph and another with the earthbent Willowrush Verge (which returns to battlefield when it dies), preserving Gran-Gran for its card filtering and cost reduction abilities.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 152,
      "player": "Sonnet Stoic",
      "decision_index": 127,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Chump-blocked Toph with a Duelist of the Mind (0/3) to prevent just 3 damage while at 15 life against an opponent at 4 life. The Duelist is a key win condition that could have significant power on the next attack turn with card draws.",
      "action_taken": "Blocked Toph, Hardheaded Teacher with Duelist of the Mind, losing the Duelist to save 3 life.",
      "better_line": "Take the full 5 damage (going to 10 life), preserve both Duelists of the Mind for a lethal counterattack next turn against the opponent at 4 life.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 162,
      "player": "DSV3 Libby",
      "decision_index": 134,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "At 4 life facing a Duelist of the Mind that has been dealing 3+ damage per turn, Sonnet Stoic passed with 2 open mana and Boomerang Basics in hand. Bouncing Duelist of the Mind would remove the primary threat and buy a critical turn. The Duelist could easily deal lethal next turn with draws boosting its power.",
      "action_taken": "Passed the turn without casting any spells, leaving 2 mana unused.",
      "better_line": "Cast Boomerang Basics targeting the opponent's Duelist of the Mind to bounce the main threat and survive another turn. This also triggers prowess on any Otter tokens for additional board presence.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 171,
      "player": "Sonnet Stoic",
      "decision_index": 140,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "At 2 life facing Duelist of the Mind which threatens lethal next turn, Sonnet Stoic passed without casting any spells despite having Boomerang Basics (U) available with Breeding Pool untapped to bounce the Duelist. They also potentially had Combustion Technique available depending on Artist's Talent level. Passing here likely means dying next turn.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without casting any spells",
      "better_line": "Cast Boomerang Basics targeting Duelist of the Mind to bounce it and buy a crucial turn at 2 life, or Combustion Technique if Artist's Talent level 2 made it castable for R to permanently remove the threat",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 188,
      "player": "Sonnet Stoic",
      "decision_index": 149,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Opponent is at 2 life. Duelist of the Mind's power equals cards drawn this turn (currently 1 from draw step). Casting Winternight Stories would draw 3 cards, making Duelist's power 4, enabling a lethal attack. Instead, the player appears focused on leveling Stormchaser's Talent which doesn't draw cards and doesn't enable lethal this turn.",
      "action_taken": "Chose to level up Stormchaser's Talent instead of casting Winternight Stories",
      "better_line": "Cast Winternight Stories (drawing 3 cards, discarding 2), making Duelist of the Mind's power 4, then attack for lethal against opponent at 2 life.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 194,
      "player": "DSV3 Libby",
      "decision_index": 153,
    }
  ],
